title: what I did
pid: e500b2e8-5a16-4206-919c-35c0536507e0
body: |2-
  - 2 very big (USA flag) cups barley
  - 6-ish that-sized cups water (somewhere in [5.5,6.5]
  - boiled in 12 minutes at high heat
  - reduced heat to 2.4 (wouldn't boil at heat 2).
    Boiling w/ lid.
    It has high thermal inertia -- takes a good while (5 min?)
    to stop boiling hard enough to overflow.
    Claude blames the stove and suggests moving the pot
    halfway off the burner for 2 minutes.

  - stirring every 15 minutes for 30 minutes, then every 8
